From: PB624 bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] irqchip/sun4i: allow wakeup sources (IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE)

A10/A13 only support s2idle, where the interrupt controller stays alive,
so any enabled interrupt can wake the system.  Without irq_set_wake every
wakeup-source (gpio-keys, AXP209 power key, RTC alarm) fails to arm with
-ENXIO and aborts suspend.

---
--- a/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c	2026-10-10 18:45:15.047621373 +0300
+++ b/drivers/irqchip/irq-sun4i.c	2026-10-10 18:45:15.055621633 +0300
@@ -87,7 +87,8 @@
 	.irq_eoi	= sun4i_irq_ack,
 	.irq_mask	= sun4i_irq_mask,
 	.irq_unmask	= sun4i_irq_unmask,
-	.flags		= IRQCHIP_EOI_THREADED | IRQCHIP_EOI_IF_HANDLED,
+	.flags		= IRQCHIP_EOI_THREADED | IRQCHIP_EOI_IF_HANDLED |
+			  IRQCHIP_SKIP_SET_WAKE,
 };
 
 static int sun4i_irq_map(struct irq_domain *d, unsigned int virq,
